 202                             
 203                             ; Following are offsets used by modules that test the integrity of data in 
 204                             ; CLRAM, DPRAM, or the node memory. These modules can be used even when 
 205                             ; debugging is turned off in the host. They check the integrity of data and
 206                             ; INT the host if data are inconsistent. The host then stops the other SIOP 
 207                             ; which did not INT and then hits a panic or an assert itself
 208                             ; This way all three uPs (two 53C720s and one 80860) stop and the logic
 209                             ; analyzer does not catch any unnecessary data on the local bus
 210                             
 211                             absolute OFFSETOF_PTR_MSG_OUT  = 12    ; relative to start of request table
 212                             absolute OFFSETOF_BYTES_MSG_OUT        = 16    ; relative to start of request table
 213                             
