1278                             
1279                             ; add32:  32-bit addition.  scratcha += scratchb
1280                             ; Usage:
1281                             ;      call add32
1282                             ;
1283                             ; Input:
1284                             ;      32-bits of scratchb
1285                             ;      32-bits of scratcha
1286                             ;
1287                             ; Output:
1288                             ;      32-bits of scratcha, the carry bit contains any overflow
1289                             ;
1290                             ; Returns:
1291                             ;      The carry bit has any overflow generated from the addition
1292                             ;
1293                             ; Uses:
1294                             ;      scratchb is destroyed.
1295                             ;
1296                             ; Desc:
1297                             ;      This operation is surprisingly difficult with the NCR instruction
1298                             ;      set and probably represents a major departure between NCR's intended
1299                             ;      use of the chip and Intel's requirements.
1300                             ;
1301                             ; Algorithm:
1302                             ;      Uses the "register to register move" instruction (an 8-bit move)
1303                             ;      which includes an obscure ability to add an 8-bit value.  The 8-bit
1304                             ;      value must be a constant coded into the "move" instruction.  32-bit
1305                             ;      addition requires 4 additions plus dealing with byte to byte carrys.
1306                             ;
1307                             ;      Move the 4 bytes of scratchb into the 4 instructions where +XXX
1308                             ;      appears.  +XXX is a place holder to (a) persuade the assembler to
1309                             ;      generate the right opcode and (b) provide a visual pattern in a hex
1310                             ;      dump to be sure the right place is modified.
1311                             ;
1312                             ;      Complication!  The move memory instruction is the only mechanism the
1313                             ;      NCR chip provides usable for modifying instructions.  Unfortunately,
1314                             ;      it demands the source and destination be the same number of bytes
1315                             ;      past the last 4-byte boundary.  That is, the source and destination
1316                             ;      address must have the same least significant 2 bits.  (If they are
1317                             ;      not, an "illegal instruction exception occurs.)  As the destination
1318                             ;      is always byte 1 of an instruction, scratchb1 is the only register
1319                             ;      aligned correctly.
1320                             
1321 00000DC4:                   add32:
1322 00000DC4: C0000001 00000000 00000E2D       move    memory 1, pass(REG_BASE+0x5c+1), add1+1         ; mod code for bits 8-15
1323                                                                                    ; and make B1 available
1324 00000DD0: 725C0000 00000000        move    scratchb0 to sfbr                       ; Move B0 to B1
1325 00000DD8: 6A5D0000 00000000        move    sfbr      to scratchb1
1326 00000DE0: C0000001 00000000 00000E25       move    memory 1, pass(REG_BASE+0x5c+1), add0+1         ; bits 0-7 patch
1327                             
1328 00000DEC: 725E0000 00000000        move    scratchb2 to sfbr                       ; move B2 to B1
1329 00000DF4: 6A5D0000 00000000        move    sfbr      to scratchb1
1330 00000DFC: C0000001 00000000 00000E35       move    memory 1, pass(REG_BASE+0x5c+1), add2+1         ; 16-23 patch
1331                             
1332 00000E08: 725F0000 00000000        move    scratchb3 to sfbr                       ; move B3 to B1
1333 00000E10: 6A5D0000 00000000        move    sfbr    to scratchb1
1334 00000E18: C0000001 00000000 00000E3D       move    memory 1, pass(REG_BASE+0x5c+1), add3+1         ; 24-31 patch
1335                             
1336                             absolute       XXX=127 ; place holder only--actual value is patched (above)
1337                             
1338 00000E24: 7E347F00 00000000 add0:  move    scratcha0+XXX to scratcha0      ; add bits 7-0
1339 00000E2C: 7F357F00 00000000 add1:  move    scratcha1+XXX to scratcha1 with carry   ; add bits 15-8
1340 00000E34: 7F367F00 00000000 add2:  move    scratcha2+XXX to scratcha2 with carry   ; add bits 23-16
1341 00000E3C: 7F377F00 00000000 add3:  move    scratcha3+XXX to scratcha3 with carry   ; add bits 31-24
1342 00000E44: 90080000 00000000        return
